# hugmesh-update — DEFAULT-ON host-binary auto-update poller (cadence timer).
#
# The TIMER half of the binary OS auto-update (the OpenRC hugmesh-update service
# runs one poll at boot; this cron entry re-runs it on the configured cadence).
# cronie reads /etc/cron.d — the SAME mechanism provision.sh uses for
# /etc/cron.d/hugmesh-backup + the device-registry / policy / vpn sync timers.
#
# DEFAULT-ON: installed ACTIVE by provision_update() on EVERY generated host/node +
# client image. There is NO opt-in flag — absence of a superadmin override means
# auto-update is ON. The live devops/hugmesh-update-policy ConfigMap can only
# ADJUST (cadence/window/staging) or DISABLE (enabled:false). The poller itself is
# fail-safe-to-update: an unreachable cluster / absent ConfigMap => it still pulls.
#
# The cadence below is the BAKED default (daily at 04:00). provision_update()
# REWRITES this line's schedule from the manifest's .update.cadence (and per-target/
# per-role .update.staging) so a build / superadmin can stage the rollout. The poller
# additionally enforces .update.window at runtime (so a tightened window takes effect
# live via the ConfigMap without re-imaging).
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
0 4 * * * root /usr/local/sbin/hugmesh-update >> /var/log/hugmesh-update.log 2>&1
